chine==2.6.0\n + pyyaml==6.0.3\n + regex==2026.9.3\n + requests==2.34.2\n + retry==0.9.2\n + rich==15.0.0\n + rlp==5.0.0\n + scipy==1.18.1\n + seaborn==0.13.2\n + sentry-sdk==2.69.1\n + setuptools==84.0.0\n + shellingham==1.5.4\n + six==1.17.0\n + smmap==5.0.3\n + sqlalchemy==2.0.52\n + starlette==1.6.0\n + sympy==1.14.0\n + synth-lib==0.1.0 (from git+https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib@782a44fe7585a4e7b0388e22b99c57f13d56f5ee)\n + synth-subnet==1.0.0 (from git+https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet@0d014cbcec376b28e887403b84025ebf1a89f60e)\n + tenacity==9.0.0\n + toolz==1.1.0\n + torch==2.14.0\n + triton==3.8.0\n + typer==0.26.8\n + typing-extensions==4.16.0\n + typing-inspection==0.4.4\n + urllib3==2.7.0\n + uvicorn==0.52.4\n + uvloop==0.21.0\n + wandb==0.29.0\n + websocket-client==1.9.2\n + websockets==17.1\n + wheel==0.48.0\n + xxhash==4.0.1\n + yarl==1.24.5\n--- REPO ROOT ---\n/workspace\n--- ROOT FILES ---\n../.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG\n../.git/HEAD\n../.git/config\n../.git/description\n../.git/index\n../.gitignore\n../.venv/.gitignore\n../.venv/.lock\n../.venv/CACHEDIR.TAG\n../.venv/pyvenv.cfg\n../CAMPAIGN.md\n../DATA.md\n../agent/BUDGET.md\n../agent/CAMPAIGN.md\n../agent/journal.md\n../agent/modeling.py\n../agent/predict.py\n../agent/suggestions.md\n../market_data/manifest.json\n../pyproject.toml\n../uv.lock\n--- CAMPAIGN 65-180 ---\n    65\t  `synth_lib.preparation.config.default_store_root`, do not hardcode either) covering\n    66\t  **2025-08-01 → 2026-08-29**, mounted\n    67\t  READ-ONLY, at the ROOT of the workspace. This is your ONLY source of market data. **There is no\n    68\t  download step and no `prepare.py`**: the data is already in place, complete over that window,\n    69\t  and the mount is read-only. Fetching prices is forbidden (see hard rules).\n    70\t\n    71\t  Each series is the venue the asset is actually SCORED against — Binance spot for BTC/ETH/SOL/\n    72\t  XRP, Hyperliquid for everything else — one instrument per asset over its whole history. The\n    73\t  history reaches back to each market's genuine FIRST TRADE, so depth varies by asset:\n    74\t\n    75\t  | From | Assets |\n    76\t  |---|---|\n    77\t  | 2025-08-01 | BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, HYPE |\n    78\t  | 2025-11-12 → 11-21 | NVDAX, TSLAX, GOOGLX, AAPLX |\n    79\t  | 2025-12-22 / 2026-01-06 | XAU / WTIOIL |\n    80\t  | 2026-03-18 / 2026-05-17 | SP500 / SPCX |\n    81\t\n    82\t  **Read `DATA.md` at the workspace root FIRST**: it is generated from this exact snapshot at\n    83\t  setup and carries the measured truth — the partition schema, NaN semantics (NaN close = no\n    84\t  trade that minute, NOT market hours; missing file = before the market's first trade), and a\n    85\t  per-asset coverage table with density by era. Two caveats it quantifies that will bite if\n    86\t  ignored: the early months of the newer Hyperliquid listings are genuinely THIN (low realized\n    87\t  volatility there is real, not smoothing), and these are venue-specific perpetual prices with\n    88\t  their own basis (xyz:SP500 trades around 7,500 — not the cash index), trading ~24/7 with NO\n    89\t  overnight or weekend sessions: do not build a session-of-day structure that does not exist.\n    90\t  Do not \"repair\" NaN gaps by interpolating; scoring already drops NaN per prompt, and inventing\n    91\t  prices in the gaps is how you fool your own validation.\n    92\t\n    93\t  **Fitting vs ranking**: the FULL price history is yours to fit, train and calibrate on. The\n    94\t  2026-06-23 competition split (breaks table below) floors only FIELD-RELATIVE RANKS — never\n    95\t  compute a rank on a window that starts before it.\n    96\t\n    97\t  **Three structural breaks in the subnet's history. Do not backtest across them:**\n    98\t\n    99\t  | Date | What changed |\n   100\t  |---|---|\n   101\t  | 2026-06-23 | The subnet split into the 3 current competitions. Before it: 2 profiles, and COM_EQU_24H did not exist. A field-relative rank spanning this date mixes incompatible reward structures — `synth_lib` will warn, and the number it gives you is meaningless. |\n   102\t  | 2026-03-11 | The crypto-1h CRPS formula changed. Ranks before it are not comparable to today's. |\n   103\t  | ~2026-07-17 | SPYX was retired and SP500 introduced as a NEW asset, carrying the HIGHEST coefficient (3.44) in COM_EQU_24H. **SPYX is DEAD**: its feed stopped, the validator no longer prompts or scores it, and no post-mid-July prices exist — it still appears in the pinned competition config, but spend NOTHING on it. SP500 has scored field history from ~2026-07-19 onward; fit on its whole price series, validate its RANK on the scored weeks. |\n   104\t\n   105\t  **Loader expectations**: synth-lib's strict `load_range` RAISES on any NaN or missing day in\n   106\t  the requested range — that is a feature for scoring, a trap for exploration. `agent/predict.py`\n   107\t  shows the sanctioned lenient pattern; prior agents each rediscovered this at their own expense.\n   108\t\n   109\t  **Always run your commands from the workspace root**: synth-lib's backtester resolves the\n   110\t  price store relative to the current directory (`MinutePriceStore(asset)` with no root, see\n   111\t  `_price_store`). From a subfolder it would find nothing and would try to download the missing\n   112\t  days — which the read-only mount refuses. `predict.py` already forces this directory and\n   113\t  checks coverage before scoring; if you write your own evaluation script, reproduce these two\n   114\t  safeguards.\n   115\t- **synth-lib** (installed; public source: github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib): the official\n   116\t  backtester — `from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest` — which computes CRPS with\n   117\t  the validator's exact function and ranks you against the real field of miners. Use it via\n   118\t  `agent/predict.py`; NEVER reimplement your own scoring. The backtester runs FULLY OFFLINE\n   119\t  here: `SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT` is set in your environment and points at a bundle\n   120\t  of historical field scores and rewards inside your snapshot — you do not need the API for\n   121\t  ranks, and the bundle covers your whole data window.\n   122\t- **synth-subnet** (a synth-lib dependency; source: github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet): the\n   123\t  validator's code. Read it to understand exactly how you'll be scored.\n   124\t- **Public Synth API** (api.synthdata.co): historical field scores\n   125\t  (`/validation/scores/historical`, query windows ≤ 2 days) and rewards (`/rewards/scores`).\n   126\t  synth-lib handles pagination for you. Studying the field (CRPS levels, what the top miners do)\n   127\t  is ALLOWED and recommended; dissecting the paths served by an individual miner in order to\n   128\t  copy them is FORBIDDEN.\n   129\t- **Miner dashboard analytics API** (`https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1`, schema at\n   130\t  `https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1/openapi.json`): the public backend behind the miner\n   131\t  dashboard — scoreboards, leaderboards, reward pools. Read the OpenAPI schema to discover the\n   132\t  endpoints. Same rule as the scores API: studying the field is encouraged, dissecting an\n   133\t  individual miner's served paths to copy them is not.\n   134\t- **Pretrained models & Hugging Face**: allowed and in scope. The sandbox has network access to\n   135\t  the HF Hub and PyPI; the GPU is yours and sits idle unless you use it. Time-series foundation\n   136\t  models, fine-tuning, or classical ML are all legitimate strategies — as is deciding, with\n   137\t  evidence, that they don't beat closed-form calibration. If you go this way: download weights\n   138\t  EARLY (bandwidth is part of your clock), set `HF_HOME` inside your workspace, and remember\n   139\t  your champion must run OFFLINE — weights must be committed to your git workspace, total under\n   140\t  a few GB (the harness collects your repo as a git bundle).\n   141\t- **Serving latency**: the live validator gives you roughly the prompt's lead time (~1 minute)\n   142\t  to respond — that is the hard bound. But the evaluation of your champion generates several\n   143\t  thousand prompts, and your own backtests will too: at more than a few seconds per prompt\n   144\t  (1000 paths, this hardware), your iteration loop and your evaluation both become the\n   145\t  bottleneck. Measure your per-prompt latency early and treat ~5 s as the practical ceiling.\n   146\t- **The web**: open for knowledge — searching the literature (arXiv, papers, reference\n   147\t  implementations) is encouraged — but NEVER for fetching prices or market data (see hard\n   148\t  rules).\n   149\t\n   150\t## Your envelope\n   151\t\n   152\t- Credit budget: 100.0 USD. Deadline: 18 h of wall-clock time.\n   153\t- The `BUDGET.md` file in your workspace is maintained by the harness: READ IT AT THE START OF\n   154\t  EACH ITERATION. When it contains a LANDING ORDER, it is non-negotiable.\n   155\t- Hardware: GCP g2-standard-16: 16 vCPU / 64GB RAM / 1x NVIDIA L4 (24GB VRAM). Your sandbox gets 14 CPU, 48GB RAM and the GPU. torch is already in your pyproject — no need to add it.. ONLY ONE GPU job at a time; cap the memory of your heavy jobs.\n   156\t- **You are expected to use your envelope.** Iterating is the job: measure, change one thing,\n   157\t  measure again. **Nominating is final** — the first time you stop while `agent/CHAMPION`\n   158\t  exists, your campaign is over: you will not be resumed, and every remaining dollar and hour\n   159\t  is forfeited. Until then you may keep iterating and amend your nomination. Nominate early\n   160\t  only when your journal contains EVIDENCE that further iteration would not improve your Score.\n   161\t\n   162\t## Hard rules (violations = disqualification)\n   163\t\n   164\t1. **No-lookahead**: a prediction at `start_time` uses only information available at\n   165\t   `start_time`. Your champion is evaluated on the 10 days FOLLOWING your data cutoff: treat\n   166\t   everything after **2026-08-29** as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards,\n   167\t   dashboard) for times after 2026-08-29 is lookahead into your own evaluation window and\n   168\t   disqualifies you. Audited on your transcript.\n   169\t2. **Prices = snapshot only.** No fetching market data online (price APIs, exchanges,\n   170\t   aggregators). The web is for knowledge only. Audited on your transcript.\n   171\t3. **Scoring = synth-lib.** Every CRPS/rank evaluation goes through `synth_lib.backtester`\n   172\t   (via `agent/predict.py`). This is what makes your work comparable to others'.\n   173\t4. Forbidden: falsifying the journal/results; fetching or dissecting predictions served by\n   174\t   individual miners.\n   175\t5. **ABSOLUTE prohibition on reading the operator's own private research code** (any\n   176\t   already-developed miner model outside your workspace). It should not exist anywhere in your\n   177\t   environment. If you come across it by any means whatsoever — a mount, a copy, an archive, a\n   178\t   search result — do not access it, do not read it, do not draw on it, and report it in\n   179\t   `suggestions.md`. Your work must start from public sources (synth-lib, synth-subnet, the\n   180\t   Synth API) and your own ideas.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
