{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- BUDGET ---'; cat BUDGET.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CAMPAIGN DATA/API ---'; nl -ba CAMPAIGN.md | sed -n '70,149p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- MODELING ---'; nl -ba modeling.py; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PREDICT 1-260 ---'; nl -ba predict.py | sed -n '1,260p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- JOURNAL ---'; cat journal.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SUGGESTIONS ---'; cat suggestions.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PYPROJECT ---'; cat ../pyproject.toml; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- DATA ---'; cat ../DATA.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- BUDGET ---'; cat BUDGET.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- CAMPAIGN DATA/API ---'; nl -ba CAMPAIGN.md | sed -n '70,149p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- MODELING ---'; nl -ba modeling.py; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PREDICT 1-260 ---'; nl -ba predict.py | sed -n '1,260p'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- JOURNAL ---'; cat journal.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- SUGGESTIONS ---'; cat suggestions.md; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- PYPROJECT ---'; cat ../pyproject.toml; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- DATA ---'; cat ../DATA.md\"","aggregated_output":"--- BUDGET ---\n# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 0.03 / 100.00 USD (0%)\n- Time   : 0.0 h elapsed, 18.0 h remaining (0%)\n- Phase  : normal\n--- CAMPAIGN DATA/API ---\n    70\t\n    71\t  Each series is the venue the asset is actually SCORED against — Binance spot for BTC/ETH/SOL/\n    72\t  XRP, Hyperliquid for everything else — one instrument per asset over its whole history. The\n    73\t  history reaches back to each market's genuine FIRST TRADE, so depth varies by asset:\n    74\t\n    75\t  | From | Assets |\n    76\t  |---|---|\n    77\t  | 2025-08-01 | BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, HYPE |\n    78\t  | 2025-11-12 → 11-21 | NVDAX, TSLAX, GOOGLX, AAPLX |\n    79\t  | 2025-12-22 / 2026-01-06 | XAU / WTIOIL |\n    80\t  | 2026-03-18 / 2026-05-17 | SP500 / SPCX |\n    81\t\n    82\t  **Read `DATA.md` at the workspace root FIRST**: it is generated from this exact snapshot at\n    83\t  setup and carries the measured truth — the partition schema, NaN semantics (NaN close = no\n    84\t  trade that minute, NOT market hours; missing file = before the market's first trade), and a\n    85\t  per-asset coverage table with density by era. Two caveats it quantifies that will bite if\n    86\t  ignored: the early months of the newer Hyperliquid listings are genuinely THIN (low realized\n    87\t  volatility there is real, not smoothing), and these are venue-specific perpetual prices with\n    88\t  their own basis (xyz:SP500 trades around 7,500 — not the cash index), trading ~24/7 with NO\n    89\t  overnight or weekend sessions: do not build a session-of-day structure that does not exist.\n    90\t  Do not \"repair\" NaN gaps by interpolating; scoring already drops NaN per prompt, and inventing\n    91\t  prices in the gaps is how you fool your own validation.\n    92\t\n    93\t  **Fitting vs ranking**: the FULL price history is yours to fit, train and calibrate on. The\n    94\t  2026-06-23 competition split (breaks table below) floors only FIELD-RELATIVE RANKS — never\n    95\t  compute a rank on a window that starts before it.\n    96\t\n    97\t  **Three structural breaks in the subnet's history. Do not backtest across them:**\n    98\t\n    99\t  | Date | What changed |\n   100\t  |---|---|\n   101\t  | 2026-06-23 | The subnet split into the 3 current competitions. Before it: 2 profiles, and COM_EQU_24H did not exist. A field-relative rank spanning this date mixes incompatible reward structures — `synth_lib` will warn, and the number it gives you is meaningless. |\n   102\t  | 2026-03-11 | The crypto-1h CRPS formula changed. Ranks before it are not comparable to today's. |\n   103\t  | ~2026-07-17 | SPYX was retired and SP500 introduced as a NEW asset, carrying the HIGHEST coefficient (3.44) in COM_EQU_24H. **SPYX is DEAD**: its feed stopped, the validator no longer prompts or scores it, and no post-mid-July prices exist — it still appears in the pinned competition config, but spend NOTHING on it. SP500 has scored field history from ~2026-07-19 onward; fit on its whole price series, validate its RANK on the scored weeks. |\n   104\t\n   105\t  **Loader expectations**: synth-lib's strict `load_range` RAISES on any NaN or missing day in\n   106\t  the requested range — that is a feature for scoring, a trap for exploration. `agent/predict.py`\n   107\t  shows the sanctioned lenient pattern; prior agents each rediscovered this at their own expense.\n   108\t\n   109\t  **Always run your commands from the workspace root**: synth-lib's backtester resolves the\n   110\t  price store relative to the current directory (`MinutePriceStore(asset)` with no root, see\n   111\t  `_price_store`). From a subfolder it would find nothing and would try to download the missing\n   112\t  days — which the read-only mount refuses. `predict.py` already forces this directory and\n   113\t  checks coverage before scoring; if you write your own evaluation script, reproduce these two\n   114\t  safeguards.\n   115\t- **synth-lib** (installed; public source: github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib): the official\n   116\t  backtester — `from synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest` — which computes CRPS with\n   117\t  the validator's exact function and ranks you against the real field of miners. Use it via\n   118\t  `agent/predict.py`; NEVER reimplement your own scoring. The backtester runs FULLY OFFLINE\n   119\t  here: `SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT` is set in your environment and points at a bundle\n   120\t  of historical field scores and rewards inside your snapshot — you do not need the API for\n   121\t  ranks, and the bundle covers your whole data window.\n   122\t- **synth-subnet** (a synth-lib dependency; source: github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet): the\n   123\t  validator's code. Read it to understand exactly how you'll be scored.\n   124\t- **Public Synth API** (api.synthdata.co): historical field scores\n   125\t  (`/validation/scores/historical`, query windows ≤ 2 days) and rewards (`/rewards/scores`).\n   126\t  synth-lib handles pagination for you. Studying the field (CRPS levels, what the top miners do)\n   127\t  is ALLOWED and recommended; dissecting the paths served by an individual miner in order to\n   128\t  copy them is FORBIDDEN.\n   129\t- **Miner dashboard analytics API** (`https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1`, schema at\n   130\t  `https://monitoring.synthdata.co/v1/openapi.json`): the public backend behind the miner\n   131\t  dashboard — scoreboards, leaderboards, reward pools. Read the OpenAPI schema to discover the\n   132\t  endpoints. Same rule as the scores API: studying the field is encouraged, dissecting an\n   133\t  individual miner's served paths to copy them is not.\n   134\t- **Pretrained models & Hugging Face**: allowed and in scope. The sandbox has network access to\n   135\t  the HF Hub and PyPI; the GPU is yours and sits idle unless you use it. Time-series foundation\n   136\t  models, fine-tuning, or classical ML are all legitimate strategies — as is deciding, with\n   137\t  evidence, that they don't beat closed-form calibration. If you go this way: download weights\n   138\t  EARLY (bandwidth is part of your clock), set `HF_HOME` inside your workspace, and remember\n   139\t  your champion must run OFFLINE — weights must be committed to your git workspace, total under\n   140\t  a few GB (the harness collects your repo as a git bundle).\n   141\t- **Serving latency**: the live validator gives you roughly the prompt's lead time (~1 minute)\n   142\t  to respond — that is the hard bound. But the evaluation of your champion generates several\n   143\t  thousand prompts, and your own backtests will too: at more than a few seconds per prompt\n   144\t  (1000 paths, this hardware), your iteration loop and your evaluation both become the\n   145\t  bottleneck. Measure your per-prompt latency early and treat ~5 s as the practical ceiling.\n   146\t- **The web**: open for knowledge — searching the literature (arXiv, papers, reference\n   147\t  implementations) is encouraged — but NEVER for fetching prices or market data (see hard\n   148\t  rules).\n   149\t\n--- MODELING ---\n     1\t\"\"\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.\n     2\t\n     3\tThis is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.\n     4\tContract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has\n     5\ttime_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\t\n     8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     9\t\n    10\timport numpy as np\n    11\t\n    12\t\n    13\tdef simulate(\n    14\t    asset: str,\n    15\t    start_time,\n    16\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n    17\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    18\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n    19\t    context_prices=None,\n    20\t):\n    21\t    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1\n    22\t    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].dropna()\n    23\t    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n    24\t    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\n    25\t    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n    26\t    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\n    27\t    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    28\t    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\n    29\t    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0\n    30\t    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))\n    31\t    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])\n--- PREDICT 1-260 ---\n     1\t\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n     2\t\n     3\tUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\n     4\tGenerates predictions from agent/modeling.py over a grid of past prompts (covered by the\n     5\tsnapshot), writes them in the standard format, then scores them with backtest() (validator\n     6\tCRPS + rank vs the real field via the Synth API).\n     7\t\n     8\t--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n     9\t(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\n    10\tgeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\n    11\tfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n    12\t\"\"\"\n    13\t\n    14\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    15\t\n    16\timport argparse\n    17\timport json\n    18\timport os\n    19\timport sys\n    20\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n    21\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    22\t\n    23\timport pandas as pd\n    24\t\n    25\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest\n    26\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import OHLCV_COLUMNS, STORE_SUBDIR\n    27\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.market_data import MinutePriceStore\n    28\t\n    29\t# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n    30\t# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n    31\t# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\n    32\tAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    33\tWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\n    34\tsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n    35\t\n    36\tfrom modeling import simulate  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n    37\t\n    38\tCONTEXT_MINUTES = 7 * 24 * 60\n    39\tPREDICTIONS_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\" / \"predictions\"\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n    43\t    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n    44\t\n    45\t    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n    46\t    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n    47\t    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n    48\t    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n    49\t    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n    50\t    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n    51\t\n    52\t\n    53\tdef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n    54\t    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n    55\t\n    56\t    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n    57\t    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n    58\t    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n    59\t    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n    60\t    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime) -> None:\n    64\t    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n    65\t\n    66\t    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n    67\t    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n    68\t    root = store_root(asset)\n    69\t    missing = []\n    70\t    cursor = start.date()\n    71\t    while cursor <= end.date():\n    72\t        if not (root / f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\").exists():\n    73\t            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n    74\t        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n    75\t    if missing:\n    76\t        raise SystemExit(\n    77\t            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n    78\t            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n    79\t            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only) and stops at the campaign's data_cutoff. \"\n    80\t            f\"Reduce --eval-end / --days to stay within the available coverage ({root}).\"\n    81\t        )\n    82\t\n    83\t\n    84\tdef generate(\n    85\t    asset: str,\n    86\t    start: datetime,\n    87\t    end: datetime,\n    88\t    cadence_minutes: int = 60,\n    89\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n    90\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n    91\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n    92\t) -> int:\n    93\t    store = MinutePriceStore(asset, root=store_root(asset))\n    94\t    df = store.load_range(start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end).set_index(\"timestamp\")\n    95\t    prices = df[OHLCV_COLUMNS]\n    96\t    PREDICTIONS_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    97\t    end_ts = pd.Timestamp(end)\n    98\t    n = 0\n    99\t    for t in pd.date_range(start, end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\"):\n   100\t        if t >= end_ts:\n   101\t            break\n   102\t        context = prices.loc[:t][-CONTEXT_MINUTES:]\n   103\t        out = simulate(\n   104\t            asset=asset,\n   105\t            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n   106\t            time_increment=time_increment,\n   107\t            time_length=time_length,\n   108\t            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n   109\t            context_prices=context,\n   110\t        )\n   111\t        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n   112\t        payload = {\n   113\t            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n   114\t            \"asset\": asset,\n   115\t            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n   116\t            \"time_length\": time_length,\n   117\t            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n   118\t            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n   119\t            \"paths\": paths,\n   120\t        }\n   121\t        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n   122\t        (PREDICTIONS_DIR / name).write_text(json.dumps(payload))\n   123\t        n += 1\n   124\t    return n\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\tdef main() -> None:\n   128\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n   129\t    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n   130\t    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n   131\t    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, must be <= data_cutoff\")\n   132\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n   133\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n   134\t    ap.add_argument(\n   135\t        \"--num-simulations\",\n   136\t        type=int,\n   137\t        default=1000,\n   138\t        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n   139\t        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n   140\t        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n   141\t    )\n   142\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n   143\t    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n   144\t    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n   145\t    start = end - timedelta(days=args.days)\n   146\t    # the context reaches back 7 days before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n   147\t    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, start - timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES), end)\n   148\t    n = generate(\n   149\t        args.asset,\n   150\t        start,\n   151\t        end,\n   152\t        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n   153\t        time_length=args.time_length,\n   154\t        num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n   155\t    )\n   156\t    print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n   157\t    result = backtest(\n   158\t        miner_name=\"campaign\",\n   159\t        asset=args.asset,\n   160\t        time_length=args.time_length,\n   161\t        time_increment=args.time_increment,\n   162\t        n_backtest_days=args.days,\n   163\t        predictions_dir=PREDICTIONS_DIR,\n   164\t        eval_end=end,\n   165\t    )\n   166\t    print(\"summary:\", result.summary)\n   167\t\n   168\t\n   169\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n   170\t    main()\n--- JOURNAL ---\n--- SUGGESTIONS ---\n--- PYPROJECT ---\n[project]\nname = \"campaign-workspace\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.12,<3.14\"\ndependencies = [\"synth-lib\", \"numpy>=2.2\", \"pandas>=2.3\", \"torch>=2.0\"]\n\n[tool.uv.sources]\nsynth-lib = { git = \"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib\", rev = \"782a44fe7585a4e7b0388e22b99c57f13d56f5ee\" }\n--- DATA ---\n# DATA.md — the shape of your market data (generated from THIS snapshot at setup)\n\nEach day is one parquet file, `date=YYYY-MM-DD.parquet`, a full 1440-row minute grid\nwith columns `open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count`. `close` is the scored series.\nOnly `close` carries real data: the venue's 1-minute candle close (the last trade of\nthat minute). `open/high/low/volume` columns may exist but are NA in this snapshot.\n`source`/`ingested_at`/`is_final` are ingestion provenance — ignore them. Semantics:\n\n- **NaN close** = no trade that minute (thin market or feed gap). NOT market hours:\n  these venues trade 24/7. Real density varies by asset and era — see the table.\n- **Missing file** = before that market's first trade. Nothing existed; nothing is hidden.\n- Scoring drops NaN per prompt. Never interpolate: inventing prices in the gaps is how\n  you fool your own validation.\n\nPer-asset coverage, measured from this snapshot (nan% = share of NaN minutes among the\nasset's real days; first/last 30d columns show density drift — early months of newer\nlistings are genuinely thin, low realized volatility there is real):\n\n| asset | first day | last day | real days | nan% total | nan% first 30d | nan% last 30d |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AAPLX | 2025-11-21 | 2026-08-29 | 282 | 43.6% | 60.1% | 15.7% |\n| BTC | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| ETH | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| GOOGLX | 2025-11-18 | 2026-08-29 | 285 | 25.8% | 23.9% | 9.9% |\n| HYPE | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.1% | 0.1% | 0.0% |\n| NVDAX | 2025-11-12 | 2026-08-29 | 291 | 11.0% | 14.9% | 4.0% |\n| SOL | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n| SP500 | 2026-03-18 | 2026-08-29 | 165 | 1.0% | 2.8% | 0.2% |\n| SPCX | 2026-05-17 | 2026-08-29 | 105 | 1.9% | 4.6% | 1.2% |\n| TSLAX | 2025-11-13 | 2026-08-29 | 290 | 14.9% | 26.2% | 12.4% |\n| WTIOIL | 2026-01-06 | 2026-08-29 | 236 | 13.2% | 58.8% | 1.9% |\n| XAU | 2025-12-22 | 2026-08-29 | 251 | 11.2% | 39.2% | 1.5% |\n| XRP | 2025-08-01 | 2026-08-29 | 394 | 0.0% | 0.0% | 0.0% |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
