{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: agent/journal.md\n@@\n-- **Result:** Pending.\n-- **Verdict:** Pending.\n-- **Lesson:** Pending.\n+- **Result:** On 2026-08-05..07, BTC-24h mean CRPS was 1934.45 and BTC-1h was 426.85. On the late window, BTC-24h (2026-08-27..29) was 3433.61, rank 257/257, top-weight ratio 7.3e-13; BTC-1h (2026-08-26..28, shifted one day earlier because a later run requires unavailable 2026-08-30 prices) was 686.62, rank 256/257, top-weight ratio 4.8e-8. Market-only diagnostics showed the 7-day volatility estimate exceeded next-24h realized RMS volatility by roughly 10% in early August and 27% for BTC / 47% for XRP late in August, while a fast/mid/slow EWMA blend was near unit scale.\n+- **Verdict:** Discard the starter volatility estimator.\n+- **Lesson:** Small raw-CRPS disadvantages become catastrophic after prompt normalization and softmax. Regime adaptation matters more than adding complex path dynamics at this stage. The evaluator must isolate prediction directories and verify horizon coverage to avoid contaminated or out-of-snapshot runs.\n+\n+## Iteration 2 — Time-decayed gap-aware volatility\n+\n+- **Hypothesis:** A timestamp-weighted blend of 1-hour, 6-hour, and 24-hour half-life per-minute variance estimates will materially improve both formats by adapting to volatility regimes. Scaling nonconsecutive observed returns by square-root elapsed minutes should also prevent thin assets from treating multi-minute moves as one-minute shocks.\n+- **Change:** Replace equal-weight seven-day standard deviation with 45%/40%/15% variance blend at half-lives 60/360/1440 minutes. Preserve the Gaussian random-walk distribution so this iteration isolates volatility estimation. Seed each prompt deterministically to reduce Monte Carlo comparison noise.\n+- **Result:** Pending.\n+- **Verdict:** Pending.\n+- **Lesson:** Pending.\n*** Update File: agent/modeling.py\n@@\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.\n-\n-This is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.\n-Contract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has\n-time_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.\n-\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Regime-adaptive probabilistic price simulator for Synth SN50.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n@@\n import numpy as np\n+\n+\n+def _weighted_variance(returns: np.ndarray, ages: np.ndarray, half_life: float) -> float:\n+    weights = np.exp2(-ages / half_life)\n+    return float(np.sum(weights * returns * returns) / np.sum(weights))\n+\n+\n+def _per_minute_variance(context_prices, time_length: int) -> float:\n+    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].dropna().astype(float)\n+    if len(closes) < 12:\n+        return 1e-6\n+\n+    values = np.log(closes.to_numpy())\n+    timestamps = closes.index\n+    elapsed_minutes = np.asarray(\n+        (timestamps[1:] - timestamps[:-1]).total_seconds() / 60.0,\n+        dtype=float,\n+    )\n+    returns = np.diff(values)\n+    valid = (\n+        np.isfinite(returns)\n+        & np.isfinite(elapsed_minutes)\n+        & (elapsed_minutes > 0)\n+        & (elapsed_minutes <= 60)\n+    )\n+    if valid.sum() < 10:\n+        return 1e-6\n+\n+    returns = returns[valid] / np.sqrt(elapsed_minutes[valid])\n+    return_times = timestamps[1:][valid]\n+    ages = np.asarray(\n+        (timestamps[-1] - return_times).total_seconds() / 60.0,\n+        dtype=float,\n+    )\n+    fast = _weighted_variance(returns, ages, 60.0)\n+    medium = _weighted_variance(returns, ages, 360.0)\n+    slow = _weighted_variance(returns, ages, 1440.0)\n+    if time_length <= 3600:\n+        weights = (0.55, 0.35, 0.10)\n+    else:\n+        weights = (0.45, 0.40, 0.15)\n+    variance = weights[0] * fast + weights[1] * medium + weights[2] * slow\n+    return max(float(variance), 1e-12)\n@@\n-    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].dropna()\n+    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].dropna()\n     last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n-    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\n-    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n-    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\n-    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n+    variance = _per_minute_variance(context_prices, time_length)\n+    per_step_sigma = np.sqrt(variance * (time_increment / 60.0))\n+    seed = hash((asset, str(start_time), time_increment, time_length)) & 0xFFFFFFFF\n+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ngit add agent/modeling.py agent/predict.py agent/journal.md && git commit -m \\\"establish adaptive volatility baseline\\\" && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
